        "original_id": "f58f663e-661e-547f-998a-a5f5347ee466",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nick Offerman, Gary Winick, Michael Ealy, Nora Dunn, Anne Archer, Matthew Carey\n- Films: November, Tadpole, 13 Going on 30, Pieces of April\n- Organizations: Sundance Film Festival, NBC, Television Critics Association, InDigEnt\n- Roles: actor, voice actor, producer, writer, comedian, carpenter, filmmaker, director\n\nFacts:\n- Gary Winick was an American filmmaker born on March 31, 1961, and he died on February 27, 2011.\n- Nick Offerman was born on June 26, 1970, and he is an American actor, voice actor, producer, writer, comedian, and carpenter.\n- Gary Winick directed the films Tadpole in 2002 and 13 Going on 30 in 2004.\n- Gary Winick produced Pieces of April in 2003 and November in 2004 through his New York City-based independent film production company InDigEnt.\n- November is a 2004 American psychological thriller film that was first screened at the 2004 Sundance Film Festival.\n- November co-stars Michael Ealy, Nora Dunn, Anne Archer, Nick Offerman, and Matthew Carey.\n- Nick Offerman is widely known for his breakout role as Ron Swanson in the NBC sitcom Parks and Recreation.\n- Nick Offerman received the Television Critics Association Award for Individual Achievement in Comedy for Parks and Recreation.",
